# Project Context
This is an Age of Empires 2-inspired RTS game with:
- Java Spring Boot backend (WebSocket support)
- HTML/JS front end
- RMS (Random Map Script) generation system
- Real-time multiplayer functionality

# Coding Standards

## Java/Spring Boot
- Use Spring Boot 3.x conventions
- REST endpoints follow /api/{resource} pattern
- WebSocket endpoints use /ws/{topic}
- Service layer handles business logic
- Controllers are thin, delegating to services
- Use constructor injection for dependencies
- Prefer records for DTOs

## Frontend/JavaScript
- Use modern ES6+ syntax
- Async/await over promise chains
- Descriptive variable names (e.g., landTiles, terrainTypes)
- Canvas-based visualizations for game rendering

## RMS Generation
- Follow Age of Empires 2 RMS syntax conventions
- Support all major sections: PLAYER_SETUP, LAND_GENERATION, TERRAIN_DEFINITION, etc.
- Use organic growth algorithms for realistic terrain
- Stream generation progress via WebSocket
**See documents/rms_guide.md for complete RMS reference and syntax**

# Architecture Preferences
- RESTful for state changes
- WebSocket for real-time updates
- Binary encoding for performance-critical data (map tiles)
- Clean separation: controllers → services → repositories
- SOLID principles

# File Organization
- Backend: src/main/java/com/{package}/
- Frontend: src/main/resources/static/ or separate React app
- Tests mirror source structure

**see documents/promtingguid.md on how to make promots**